FreeVT Change Log by Jochen (31-8-95)

Changes from 0.5c.2 to make 0.5c.3
All changes are REMed with New3!! so that everyone can find them...
0.5c.3 distributed 31-August-95
10.Changed p$ and q$ in freevt: from 2 to 255 to cure the String to Long 
   error that Alan and I experienced. This needs further looking into to 
   find the cause of the error.
9. Reduced the code required to load preference file at the start of 
   the freevt: procedure
8. Changed the APP name from freevt to FreeVT as this looks nicer
   under the icon when you have no *.fvt files
7. Added cursor option to screen menu, with settings stored bit-mapped 
   in a new global variable curs%.
   Main changes are in vtmenu: and all cursor settings are now done in 
   the new setcurs: procedure. If you need to set the cursor just call
   setcurs:
   Added the cursor setting to the savep: and loadp: procs so that the
   cursor is saved in the setup file
6. Combined delete: and backs: procedures into one (as they are so
   similar, this avoids redundancy of code) with a switch to enable 
   the delete function.
   New procedure is bsdel:(del) where del%=TRUE (-1) to delete.
   Delete works by going back one col%, printing a space, and then
   going back once col% again.
5. Changed the capture filename to fvtcap.txt, so as not to overwrite
   capture.txt (when I get this finished, that is). Still doesn't do 
   anything, but it's next on the list
4. Changed the save and load settings file name in vtmenu to CMD$(2).
   This means that the current filename will always appear in the dialog
   box when saving, or loading a file. This is much neater
3. Got the local echo working well - changes are to freevt:, to loadp: and
   savep:, and to vtmenu:.
   Two new procedures are included - these are used in loadp, savep, and
   vtmenu. They will also be used in the capture routine, when ready.
   The new procs are cvthxs:() and cvtshx:(), being convert hex to string
   and string to hex respectively. These procedures are heavily commented
   and if anyone knows a way to reduce the code please let me know.
2. Trapped the LOPEN to generate a nicer alert dialog when an error
   occurs during startup (link not plugged in, etc)
1. Fixed the bug with the databits not showing correct in the 
   serial port dialog. (when it was 7, dialog showed 8, & 6 showed 5)


